Rules:
- One central theme, usually 3–6 distinct main branches; use fewer if warranted.
- Organize relationships, concepts, methods, findings and limitations as relevant.
- At most 4 levels including the root, 65 nodes total, and 8 children per node.
- Labels: concise Vietnamese, at most 120 characters. Descriptions: 1–3 sentences,
